# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Brier · 0G MAINNET (chain 16661)
#
#  Copy to .env.mainnet, fill in, then:  chmod 600 .env.mainnet
#  scripts/deploy-mainnet.sh reads this file in preference to .env, so the
#  Galileo config keeps working and no mainnet key ever sits beside the
#  testnet deployer key that was burned into a transcript on 2026-08-30.
#
#  TWO KINDS OF ENTRY, and the difference is the whole point of this file:
#
#    🔑 PRIVATE KEY   this machine signs with it. 0x + 64 hex characters.
#    📬 ADDRESS ONLY  0x + 40 hex. Nothing here can spend it; the wallet signs
#                     for itself, elsewhere, when it chooses to.
#
#  If you paste a private key next to a 📬 line you have handed this machine a
#  wallet it was never supposed to hold. If you paste an address next to a 🔑
#  line the script refuses it by shape before it sends anything.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 🔑 PRIVATE KEYS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 🔑 DEPLOYER_KEY — deploys the protocol. REQUIRED.
#
# A KEY THAT HAS NEVER BEEN USED. Not the Galileo one: that was printed into a
# terminal transcript by a `bash -x` run, and deploy-mainnet.sh refuses it by
# address, so a paste of it fails rather than deploys.
#
# It needs about 0.2 0G. The deploy measured 36,787,692 gas — 0.147 0G at 4 gwei
# — and the script demands 45M gas' worth of headroom before it starts.
#
# This key is not a role you keep. It is important for about ten minutes and
# then irrelevant: ownership moves to the timelock and it becomes inert. Retire
# it afterwards.
DEPLOYER_KEY=

# 🔑 CURATOR_KEY — signs the EIP-712 approval that lets a market be created.
#
# THE ONE PAIR WHERE YOU NEED BOTH FORMS. This key's address must equal
# CURATOR_SIGNER below, because the contract checks the signature against that
# address and nothing reconciles the two for you — a mismatch fails at
# createMarket with BadCuratorSignature, after the curator has already signed.
#
# It is also the whole of your exposure control: no market exists on your
# deployment unless this key signed for it.
CURATOR_KEY=

# 🔑 KEEPER_KEY — closes markets and opens resolutions. ITS OWN WALLET.
#
# Every call it makes is permissionless, so it needs gas and nothing else. Give
# it its own key anyway: a keeper runs unattended on a box that is online all
# the time, and it is the last wallet that should also be able to deploy.
#
# Run at least two keepers, on separate hosts, with separate keys. They race
# harmlessly — each simulates before it sends.
KEEPER_KEY=

# 🔑 UPLOADER_KEY — pays 0G Storage for MarketSpec and receipt uploads.
#
# May be the same wallet as the curator or the keeper; it only needs gas. Kept
# separate here so that the wallet writing documents is not the one signing
# market approvals, if you would rather they were not the same.
UPLOADER_KEY=

# 🔑 GOVERNANCE_KEY — LEAVE EMPTY unless governance is a hot key.
#
# scripts/handover.sh --unsigned prints the calldata for a Safe to submit, which
# is the form to use when governance is a multisig — no governance key ever goes
# near this machine. Fill this in only if you have accepted that governance is a
# single hot key, and know that one stolen key then rewrites the protocol with a
# 48-hour delay as the only alarm.
GOVERNANCE_KEY=


# ── 📬 ADDRESSES ONLY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# All four are REQUIRED, must be four DISTINCT addresses, and none may be the
# deployer's. GOVERNANCE must differ from GUARDIAN. DeployLib.resolveRoles
# refuses every one of those, and deploy-mainnet.sh refuses them first with a
# message that names the variable.

# 📬 GOVERNANCE — proposer and executor on the timelock. Every parameter, every
# upgrade, after a 48-hour delay. USE A SAFE. The script cannot check that it is
# a multisig and will not try; a single EOA here means one stolen key eventually
# owns the protocol.
GOVERNANCE=

# 📬 GUARDIAN — may pause() and void() a market that has not closed. Deliberately
# outside the timelock, because fast action must not need the key that rewrites
# the rules. It cannot move funds and cannot change an outcome.
GUARDIAN=

# 📬 TREASURY — receives the protocol's share of fees, slashed stake, and
# whatever sweepUnclaimed collects after a year. It never signs anything.
TREASURY=

# 📬 CURATOR_SIGNER — the address the contract checks CURATOR_KEY's signature
# against. Derive it rather than typing it:
#     cast wallet address --private-key "$CURATOR_KEY"
CURATOR_SIGNER=

# 📬 COLLATERAL — the token markets settle in. W0G, wrapped native 0G.
#
# Verified on chain 2026-08-31: 18 decimals, backed 1:1 exactly (the contract's
# native balance equalled totalSupply to the wei), deposit()/withdraw() in the
# WETH9 shape, mint() permissioned, and no upgradeTo / pause / blacklist / owner
# anywhere in its bytecode. Nothing can change what it does.
#
# The alternative is USDC.e 0x1f3aa82227281ca364bfb3d253b0f1af1da6473e — 6
# decimals, upgradeable, and pausable by a single key. A paused token reverts
# inside safeTransfer, where Brier has no say, so the promise that a pause never
# blocks an exit stops holding end to end. There is no USDT on this chain.
#
# DO NOT paste 0x4B948d64dE1F71fCd12fB586f4c776421a35b3eE. 0G's docs give it as
# bridged 0G on Ethereum and BNB and it also carries 12,611 bytes of code here,
# so it looks live — but decimals() reverts and it is not a token on 16661.
COLLATERAL=0x1cd0690ff9a693f5ef2dd976660a8dafc81a109c

# 📬 ZG_PROVIDERS — 0G Compute providers, comma-separated, one per committee seat.
#
# LEAVE AS IS OR CHOOSE YOUR OWN, but do not reduce it to one. With a single
# provider every committee member runs the same model over the same evidence at
# temperature 0, which makes them one deterministic function evaluated N times:
# they cannot disagree. On 2026-08-31 that carried a wrong settlement to chain
# three votes to nil.
#
# The three below are TeeML-attested text models — GLM-5-FP8, qwen3.7-plus and
# gpt-5.4-mini. Mainnet lists seven; see the current catalogue with
#     CHAIN_ID=16661 npx tsx examples/providers.ts
# claude-opus-5 and claude-fable-5 appear there with `standard` verifiability
# rather than TeeML, so resolve.ts refuses their answers. Do not count them.
#
# EACH provider needs its own funded sub-account and TEE acknowledgement:
#     node scripts/setup-compute.mjs --provider 0x…     (1 0G apiece)
ZG_PROVIDERS=0xd9966e13a6026Fcca4b13E7ff95c94DE268C471C,0x1B3AAef3ae5050EEE04ea38cD4B087472BD85EB0,0x25F8f01cA76060ea40895472b1b79f76613Ca497

# 📬 ERC8004_IDENTITY / ERC8004_REPUTATION — LEAVE EMPTY ON MAINNET.
#
# Both canonical addresses hold an ERC-1967 proxy with an empty implementation
# slot on 16661: 130 bytes of code, so a liveness check on code alone passes,
# and every call through them reverts. Wiring them produces a deployment that
# fails much later at linkErc8004. Unset means reputation publishing is simply
# off, which _publish tolerates and settlement never notices. Governance can set
# them if the registries are ever brought up.
ERC8004_IDENTITY=
ERC8004_REPUTATION=

# 📬 RESOLVER — LEAVE EMPTY. The direct-settlement bypass, which exists for
# testnet lifecycles. A market settled through it records viaCommittee == false.
RESOLVER=


# ── knobs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ZERO_G_MAINNET_RPC=https://evmrpc.0g.ai
CHAIN_ID=16661
# 48 hours. Every administrative act costs this long once the handover is done.
TIMELOCK_DELAY=172800

# ── Money parameters, in the collateral's OWN BASE UNITS ─────────────────────
# One W0G is 1000000000000000000. Leave a line at 0 or delete it to keep the
# protocol default, which is written in WHOLE TOKENS: stake 100, bond 50,
# seed 100, deposit 20, min trade 1.
#
# The defaults are the right long-run policy and the wrong launch cost —
# fourteen resolvers at a 100-token stake lock 2,800 W0G before a single market
# exists. At 1 W0G the same roster costs 28.
#
# The simulation echoes every one of these back in whole tokens before it
# broadcasts. Read that line; it is what catches a wrong exponent.
MIN_RESOLVER_STAKE=1000000000000000000
DISPUTE_BOND=1000000000000000000
MIN_SEED=1000000000000000000
MIN_SETTLEMENT_DEPOSIT=1000000000000000000
# 0.01 W0G, NOT 1. A minimum trade equal to the seed would forbid every trade
# smaller than the entire book; the deploy refuses that outright.
MIN_TRADE_TOKENS=10000000000000000
